<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pura Luhur Uluwatu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uluwatu Temple</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pura Luhur Uluwatu is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> sea temple on a clifftop at the south-western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, one of the island's principal directional temples. It is associated with the 16th-century priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dang-hyang-nirartha">Dang Hyang Nirartha</a>, who is said to have attained spiritual liberation there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pura-luhur-uluwatu.jpg" alt="Pura Luhur Uluwatu" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paskuu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pura_Luhur_Uluwatu_2017-08-17_(34).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
